00:03:07.790 --> 00:03:11.930
Kanade-kun, do you know the 
definition of a one meter unit?

00:03:12.320 --> 00:03:13.960
Um...

00:03:13.960 --> 00:03:17.200
It's about three times the 
length of this... right?

00:03:17.210 --> 00:03:21.970
<b>Radius r</b>

00:03:17.210 --> 00:03:21.970
<b>Center (a, b)</b>

00:03:17.430 --> 00:03:18.440
Yes.

00:03:18.440 --> 00:03:21.950
But don't you wonder why it's that length?

00:03:21.970 --> 00:03:30.730
m 0 0 l 150 0 l 150 75 l 0 75

00:03:21.970 --> 00:03:30.730
<b>1/10,000,000 
of this length
\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\his 1m</b>

00:03:21.970 --> 00:03:30.730
m 0 0 l 50 0 l 50 24 l 0 24

00:03:21.970 --> 00:03:30.730
<b>North Pole</b>

00:03:21.970 --> 00:03:30.730
m 0 0 l 50 0 l 50 24 l 0 24

00:03:21.970 --> 00:03:30.730
<b>Equator</b>

00:03:22.500 --> 00:03:25.830
At first, in 1790 in France,

00:03:25.830 --> 00:03:28.690
they decided it would be 
1/10,000,000 of the distance

00:03:28.690 --> 00:03:30.730
between the North Pole and the Equator.

00:03:30.730 --> 00:03:36.480
This
\h\h\h\hwill be 1m

00:03:30.730 --> 00:03:36.480
m 0 0 l 190 0 l 190 40 l 0 40

00:03:30.730 --> 00:03:36.480
<b>Standard Meter</b>

00:03:30.730 --> 00:03:36.480
(Platinum iridium alloy)

00:03:30.730 --> 00:03:37.110
In 1889, physical standard meters were created 
as the basis for a one meter measurement.

00:03:37.110 --> 00:03:41.370
However, they would expand, 
causing issues with measurement,

00:03:37.230 --> 00:03:41.360
m 0 0 l 80 0 l 80 35 l 0 35

00:03:37.230 --> 00:03:41.360
<b>Shift</b>

00:03:37.230 --> 00:03:41.360
m 0 0 l 68 0 l 68 35 l 0 35

00:03:37.230 --> 00:03:41.360
<b>Expansion</b>

00:03:41.370 --> 00:03:43.250
so our current definition is...

00:03:43.240 --> 00:03:58.750
m 0 0 l 68 0 l 68 35 l 0 35

00:03:43.240 --> 00:03:58.750
<b>Earth</b>

00:03:43.240 --> 00:03:58.750
m 0 0 l 270 0 l 270 35 l 0 35

00:03:43.240 --> 00:03:58.750
<b>299,792,458m/s</b>

00:03:43.830 --> 00:03:52.740
the distance traveled by light in 
a vacuum in 1/299,792,456 of a second.

00:03:53.250 --> 00:03:58.760
It was defined using the speed of light 
in a vacuum, which is a constant.

00:03:59.060 --> 00:04:00.880
That's kind of amazing.

00:04:00.880 --> 00:04:04.620
Units change like this 
according to the times.

00:04:00.880 --> 00:04:08.640
<b></b>Equation of a Circle

00:04:00.880 --> 00:04:08.640
<b>Radius r</b>

00:04:00.880 --> 00:04:08.640
<b>Center (a, b)</b>

00:04:04.620 --> 00:04:08.630
They're things which someone simply 
decided upon for convenience.

00:04:09.080 --> 00:04:12.390
One day, maybe something 
completely unexpected...

00:04:12.800 --> 00:04:15.310
will have units assigned to it.

00:04:17.320 --> 00:04:20.040
<i>Whenever I see his face, my heart races.</i>

00:04:20.610 --> 00:04:23.660
<i>I come to him every day 
like this with questions,</i>

00:04:23.940 --> 00:04:27.160
<i>and I'm only lonely on the weekends 
because I can't see him.</i>

00:04:27.410 --> 00:04:29.660
<i>This feeling of mine...</i>

00:04:29.980 --> 00:04:32.780
<i>if there were units, 
could it be measured, too?</i>

00:04:33.570 --> 00:04:37.230
When we think of this example 
from Kanade's high school years,

00:04:33.660 --> 00:04:40.170
Proof 7
Science-types Fell in Love, 
So They Tried Going on a Group Date.

00:04:37.230 --> 00:04:40.430
all of the parameters of Kanade's love...

00:04:40.420 --> 00:04:44.170
• Frequency with which looking at the face causes palpitations 1/1
 • Number of times they absolutely must meet in one day 1 time
 • Period of time in which not meeting causes loneliness 48 hours

00:04:40.420 --> 00:04:44.170
(1 Kanade love power)

00:04:41.030 --> 00:04:43.030
comprise one Kanade love power.

00:04:43.030 --> 00:04:44.170
Wha?!

00:04:44.450 --> 00:04:46.040
Outside of formulas,

00:04:46.040 --> 00:04:48.440
it may be abbreviated as Kanade-love.

00:04:48.440 --> 00:04:51.030
How did I become the base reference?

00:04:51.030 --> 00:04:53.560
Also, did I tell you about 
that incident, Senpai?

00:04:53.560 --> 00:04:55.850
I heard it from you before, 
when we were drinking.

00:04:55.850 --> 00:04:57.440
What did I do?!

00:04:57.860 --> 00:05:00.380
The unit of measure for human 
favor and affection...

00:05:00.380 --> 00:05:04.460
We wanted something that was both 
normal for us and easy to visualize.

00:05:04.700 --> 00:05:07.810
You are the most conventional 
person in this lab.

00:05:07.810 --> 00:05:10.190
Your parameters lean towards 
those of other people!

00:05:10.190 --> 00:05:11.640
I can't refute that.

00:05:12.130 --> 00:05:13.340
Which means that...

00:05:13.740 --> 00:05:17.200
in feeling lonely for Aika after 
three hours, my feelings are...

00:05:17.490 --> 00:05:19.020
Sixteen Kanade-loves.

00:05:19.020 --> 00:05:20.130
Exactly!

00:05:20.130 --> 00:05:22.700
Kosuke-kun, you don't need to join in, too!

00:05:23.160 --> 00:05:26.240
My heart races three times out of 
five when looking at her face.

00:05:26.240 --> 00:05:30.690
So the frequency of face induced 
palpitations is 0.6 Kanade-loves.

00:05:30.690 --> 00:05:34.390
Every parameter can be expressed 
through a number of Kanades.

00:05:34.390 --> 00:05:36.330
And if we're able to formulate 
a more detailed definition,

00:05:36.330 --> 00:05:38.480
every kind of love will be able to be 
expressed through numerical values.

00:05:38.850 --> 00:05:39.970
Wow.

00:05:40.410 --> 00:05:43.410
All the love in the world can be 
expressed through Kanade-love!

00:05:42.610 --> 00:05:46.360
269 Kanade-love 858 Kanade-love 208 Kanade-love 153 Kanade-love 91 Kanade-love
498 Kanade-love 384 Kanade-love 322 Kanade-love 973 Kanade-love 267 Kanade-love
856 Kanade-love 664 Kanade-love 206 Kanade-love 230 Kanade-love 664 Kanade-love
