00:05:43.410 --> 00:05:46.370
Yes. The world is filled to 
the brim with Kanade-love.

00:05:46.400 --> 00:05:47.610
<b>Force of Impact</b>

00:05:46.700 --> 00:05:47.610
<b>Force of Impact</b>

00:05:47.600 --> 00:05:50.620
Think a little harder about 
how you phrase things.

00:05:51.370 --> 00:05:53.300
I'm sorry, Kanade-chan.

00:05:53.300 --> 00:05:56.910
But this unit might become the 
key to our romance research.

00:05:56.910 --> 00:05:57.370
What?

00:05:58.470 --> 00:06:00.720
Our new research.

00:06:00.720 --> 00:06:03.760
I'd be pleased if you'd 
help us, Kanade-chan.

00:06:03.760 --> 00:06:06.400
<i>Himuro-senpai looks really happy.</i>

00:06:06.400 --> 00:06:07.520
<i>Of course she does.</i>

00:06:07.520 --> 00:06:11.270
<i>She's happy to be doing research 
with Yukimura-senpai again.</i>

00:06:11.270 --> 00:06:13.490
<i>Oh, I don't want to throw a 
wet blanket over everything!</i>

00:06:13.490 --> 00:06:15.920
<i>I want to help her!</i>

00:06:15.920 --> 00:06:17.670
Yes! Please, Kanade!

00:06:17.670 --> 00:06:19.210
For the sake of Kanade-love!

00:06:19.210 --> 00:06:22.010
<i>But this "Kanade-love" thing 
is a no! Not "Kanade-love"!</i>

00:06:22.010 --> 00:06:23.760
Please help us with the Kanade-love.

00:06:23.760 --> 00:06:25.340
Kanade-love is great!

00:06:25.340 --> 00:06:26.410
Kanade-love!

00:06:27.780 --> 00:06:32.610
Please let me think about it a little!

00:06:30.420 --> 00:06:31.530
Wait, Kanade-love!

00:06:31.530 --> 00:06:32.880
What's wrong, Kanade-love-chan?

00:06:32.880 --> 00:06:34.030
Kanade-lovecchi!

00:06:34.030 --> 00:06:35.870
Where are you going, Kanade-love?

00:06:35.870 --> 00:06:37.720
Kanade-love!

00:06:37.090 --> 00:06:38.790
Stop saying Kanade-love!

00:06:45.180 --> 00:06:47.470
I'm sorry! Were you waiting long?

00:06:48.050 --> 00:06:50.770
It's fine. I just got here.

00:06:50.770 --> 00:06:53.760
But, um... This exchange 
feels sort of like a date.

00:06:54.140 --> 00:06:57.020
You're right! It happens 
all the time, doesn't it?

00:06:57.300 --> 00:07:02.280
<i>Yes. This must be how regular 
people go on a date.</i>

00:07:02.470 --> 00:07:04.670
<i>It's absolutely not like that over there.</i>

00:07:04.670 --> 00:07:05.280
Look!

00:07:05.280 --> 00:07:09.540
Up to this point is within three meters of 
the fountain where we're supposed to meet.

00:07:09.540 --> 00:07:13.530
At ten o' clock, zero minutes, and zero 
seconds, your feet were not within this radius.

00:07:13.760 --> 00:07:14.770
That's not true!

00:07:14.770 --> 00:07:17.760
And, Yukimura-kun, the speed of 
your measuring reflex is too slow.

00:07:17.760 --> 00:07:21.290
Being 0.31 seconds late is within 
the margin of error anyway!

00:07:21.290 --> 00:07:22.290
It's unacceptable!

00:07:22.290 --> 00:07:24.540
Our time together shortens by that much!

00:07:24.540 --> 00:07:27.780
<i>I shouldn't have mentioned a double date.</i>

00:07:27.780 --> 00:07:28.780
Kanade-san.

00:07:28.780 --> 00:07:29.290
Yes?

00:07:29.510 --> 00:07:31.660
Thank you for coming today.

00:07:31.660 --> 00:07:35.300
I thought you'd just say no, 
so I'm really happy.

00:07:35.570 --> 00:07:38.670
And the way you're dressed is very cute.

00:07:38.670 --> 00:07:42.320
I-I'm glad you think so. 
I tried to dress up a little.

00:07:42.560 --> 00:07:43.530
Himuro.

00:07:44.680 --> 00:07:46.340
The way you're dressed today is...

00:07:46.980 --> 00:07:50.010
the complementary color scheme 
sets you off very well.

00:07:50.010 --> 00:07:51.810
Th-Thank you.

00:07:52.020 --> 00:07:57.520
#cdbedd and #f0e3ea really do 
look nice together, don't they?

00:07:57.520 --> 00:08:01.010
The colors around #d9b0c0 
are effective, as well.

00:08:01.010 --> 00:08:03.840
<i>Why are they speaking in hexadecimal?</i>

00:08:03.840 --> 00:08:06.250
Still, there are a lot of couples 
here today, aren't there?

00:08:06.250 --> 00:08:07.580
Yes, there are.

00:08:07.820 --> 00:08:10.990
Today, Sui, you are even 
more lovely than usual.

00:08:10.990 --> 00:08:14.840
Like a gentle breeze blowing across 
the wheat fields of Cornwall.

00:08:14.840 --> 00:08:17.230
Thank you, Chris.

00:08:17.230 --> 00:08:19.280
You're like a Chihuahua today, too.

00:08:19.280 --> 00:08:21.360
Why is it always a small breed?

00:08:21.620 --> 00:08:25.270
Aika, you're shining brightly today.

00:08:25.270 --> 00:08:27.090
<i>Thank you, Ko-su-ke.</i>

00:08:27.090 --> 00:08:29.850
You got dressed up for me, didn't you?

00:08:29.850 --> 00:08:33.190
<i>It's not like I did it for you.</i>

00:08:31.920 --> 00:08:35.490
Sorry. Do you mind if I go to 
the restroom for a moment?

00:08:35.780 --> 00:08:37.100
Am I imagining it?

00:08:37.100 --> 00:08:40.080
I feel like there are a lot 
of people I know around here!

00:08:40.080 --> 00:08:41.230
It's just as you say.

00:08:41.230 --> 00:08:43.280
What, exactly, is getting started here?!

00:08:43.580 --> 00:08:46.030
A chain-style antipodal experiment.

00:08:46.040 --> 00:08:56.930
<b>A's Wall Slam</b>

00:08:46.040 --> 00:08:56.930
<b>B's Wall Slam</b>

00:08:46.040 --> 00:09:02.310
m 0 0 l 150 0 l 150 30 l 0 30

00:08:46.040 --> 00:09:02.310
m 0 0 l 150 0 l 150 30 l 0 30

00:08:46.250 --> 00:08:47.680
In an antipodal experiment,

00:08:47.680 --> 00:08:49.070
Yukimura if, for example,

00:08:49.070 --> 00:08:51.050
you want to produce a difference 
in heart rate during a wall slam,

00:08:51.050 --> 00:08:54.150
you want every other variable 
to remain constant.

00:08:54.150 --> 00:08:56.930
However, in romance experiments 
that is very difficult.

00:08:56.930 --> 00:08:58.910
When various couples go on dates,

00:08:56.930 --> 00:09:02.310
<b>Couple A</b>

00:08:56.930 --> 00:09:02.310
<b>Couple B</b>

00:08:56.930 --> 00:09:02.310
m 0 0 l 140 0 l 140 60 l 0 60

00:08:56.930 --> 00:09:02.310
m 0 0 l 150 0 l 150 60 l 0 60

00:08:56.930 --> 00:09:02.310
<b>Crowd
Cold</b>

00:08:56.930 --> 00:09:02.310
<b>Alone
Hot</b>

00:08:58.910 --> 00:09:02.300
they will never experience 
the same conditions.

00:09:02.530 --> 00:09:05.650
Which is why the double date 
you proposed is a good idea.

00:09:05.650 --> 00:09:07.930
It makes it easier to assemble 
similar conditions.

00:09:07.930 --> 00:09:12.330
However, in our research, we need to 
compare as much data as possible.

00:09:12.740 --> 00:09:17.250
So we had 10 couples we found 
on campus participate.

00:09:17.250 --> 00:09:18.820
<i>Ten couples?</i>

00:09:18.820 --> 00:09:21.710
Ten couples lined up, 
with Kanade's couple leading the way.

00:09:21.710 --> 00:09:24.650
And each couple will do the same 
thing the pair in front of them did.

00:09:24.650 --> 00:09:27.460
This way, we won't interfere 
with your date either, right?

00:09:27.820 --> 00:09:29.690
Then, could it be...

00:09:29.690 --> 00:09:31.580
all the couples here are...

00:09:31.830 --> 00:09:35.830
I'm here at the meeting place, 
but what is it we're supposed to do?

00:09:31.920 --> 00:09:35.840
<b>Saitama University Teaching Department</b>

00:09:32.550 --> 00:09:35.840
<b>Kamiya Madoka</b>

00:09:32.840 --> 00:09:35.840
m 0 0 l 225 0 l 225 115 l 0 115

00:09:35.830 --> 00:09:40.340
We follow that couple and have fun 
in the same places they go to.

00:09:36.170 --> 00:09:40.350
<b>Saitama University Teaching Department</b>

00:09:36.800 --> 00:09:40.350
<b>Taniguchi Shouki</b>

00:09:37.090 --> 00:09:40.350
m 0 0 l 225 0 l 225 115 l 0 115

00:09:40.340 --> 00:09:42.200
What a weird experiment.

00:09:42.200 --> 00:09:45.680
They said they'd pay us, so I joined 
up, thinking of it like a side job,

00:09:45.680 --> 00:09:47.520
but if playing along with 
something this boring

00:09:47.520 --> 00:09:49.980
gives people the wrong idea 
about me, that would be awful.

00:09:49.980 --> 00:09:52.200
<i>Kamiya-san's angry.</i>

00:09:52.550 --> 00:09:57.370
<i>Being on a date experiment with a 
guy like me wouldn't be any fun.</i>

00:09:58.080 --> 00:10:01.730
<i>The least I can do is try not to 
cause Kamiya-san any problems!</i>

00:10:02.210 --> 00:10:06.500
So, Kanade-chan, you don't have to worry 
about anything. Just enjoy your date.

00:10:06.500 --> 00:10:11.880
<b>Grand Procession
of Couples</b>

00:10:06.500 --> 00:10:11.880
<b>Grand Procession
of Couples</b>

00:10:06.720 --> 00:10:10.240
Ten couples will follow you 
and do as you do. That's all.

00:10:10.240 --> 00:10:11.890
That makes me worried, though.

00:10:11.890 --> 00:10:14.040
Enough! Hurry up and go back to your date!

00:10:14.040 --> 00:10:14.940
Everyone behind you is stuck where they are!

00:10:14.940 --> 00:10:16.520
Fine! I understand!

00:10:20.090 --> 00:10:21.000
Oh!

00:10:21.260 --> 00:10:22.240
Welcome back.

00:10:22.240 --> 00:10:24.850
I'm sorry to keep you waiting.

00:10:24.850 --> 00:10:26.810
Huh? Are you all right?

00:10:26.810 --> 00:10:29.020
You seem really tired.

00:10:29.020 --> 00:10:30.670
I'm completely fine!

00:10:30.670 --> 00:10:32.010
Well, should we go?

00:10:33.090 --> 00:10:34.040
Yes, we should.

00:10:36.030 --> 00:10:39.270
<i>Yes. Right now, I should focus on my date.</i>

00:10:39.520 --> 00:10:43.020
<i>He's told me that he 
wants to go out with me.</i>

00:10:43.370 --> 00:10:48.230
<i>I don't want to disappoint him, so I need 
to have a normal date where he has fun.</i>

00:10:50.450 --> 00:10:52.040
I can't decide.

00:10:52.240 --> 00:10:55.200
Shikijou-san, do you have a favorite color?

00:10:55.200 --> 00:10:56.580
Red, maybe?

00:10:56.580 --> 00:10:59.560
But red colors tend to give 
a bold impression, right?

00:11:00.030 --> 00:11:02.680
I think something a little 
bold would look good on you.

00:11:02.680 --> 00:11:04.300
Why don't you try putting it on?

00:11:04.680 --> 00:11:06.800
Then, I'll go try it on.

00:11:07.510 --> 00:11:09.810
Which do you think is better?

00:11:14.980 --> 00:11:18.160
Hurry up and decide! You're really so slow!

00:11:18.160 --> 00:11:19.560
S-Sorry.

00:11:19.560 --> 00:11:23.370
